## Ingredients

- 4 frozen salmon fillets (about 6 oz each)
- 2 tbsp olive oil
- 1 tsp kosher salt
- 1/2 tsp black pepper
- 1 tsp garlic powder
- 1/2 tsp paprika
- 3/4 cup Kewpie mayo
- 1/2 cup sriracha
- Splash of soy sauce
- 3-4 cups kale (enough to fill the pan around the salmon)
- Panko (enough for a solid covering on each fillet)

## Steps

1. Heat the oven to 425°F. Line a metal sheet pan with foil or parchment (no glass, since it's going under the broiler).
2. Rinse the frozen fillets to remove the ice glaze and pat very dry.
3. Place skin-side down with space between them. Brush with oil and season with salt, pepper, garlic powder, and paprika.
4. Bake 12 minutes.
5. Mix the Kewpie, sriracha, and soy sauce. Pat the tops of the fillets dry and spread the sauce in a thin, even layer.
6. Bake 5-8 more minutes, until the salmon reaches 145°F.
7. Scatter the kale around the salmon and press panko over the sauce. Broil 1-2 minutes until browned and crisp. Watch closely.
8. Rest 2 minutes before serving.

